  "description": "External lighting scheme at Christ Church Peckham (676 to 680 Old Kent Road), in accordance with the enclosed Specification, Drawings, Luminaire Schedules and Lighting Calculations prepared by CES Lighting & Electrical Consultants LLP.\r\rRegard has been had for Pre-Application Advice (Reference no 26/EQ/0017) dated 23 April 2026 which aadvised that the dsign should be informed by and fully compliant with the Institute of Lighting Professionals Guidance Note GN08/23: Bats and Artificial Lighting  We obtained an Preliminary Roosting Assessment (Ecological Survey) which confirmed that the site is assessed to have low habitat value for bats. It was not considered to be a site which is suitable  as a nesting site for barn owls nor suitable to support a significant assemblage of protected and/or notable birds.\rNotwithstanding this,  we will ensure that if planning permission is granted and the external lighting proposal is implemented, the following will be carried out\r\r- install at least one bat box on the building to provide an additional roosting habitat for bats;\r- install at least one bird box onto the church will provide additional nesting habitat for birds.\r\rThe Trustees (PCC) have agreed that it needs to implement an external lighting solution at Christ Church Peckham in order to:\ri.\t improve safety for people when entering and exiting the church building via the doors at the front of the church.\rii.\t improve the church's visibility when viewed from the Old Kent Road. \riii.\timprove the church's visibility when viewed from the rear / the Ledbury Estate.\riv.\timprove safety and visibility when accessing the church from the side passage referred to at paragraph 1)(b) ?Our community? above.\rv.\tEnhance the character and appearance of our building as a local landmark in a Conservation Area which is in the process of significant development / regeneration.",
